# REN - Rename files in place

```text
REN newname=oldname
```

## Single file

Both names refer to the same drive and user. This changes the directory
name and keeps the file data in place.

```text
REN REPORT.BAK=D0:REPORT.TXT
```

## Change extensions

The source-first form accepts a destination template. With the transient
command, /DRY previews the proposed names before changing any directory
entries.

```text
:REN /DRY D0:*.DOC *.TXT
```

Check for collisions before repeating without /DRY. To transfer a file
to another drive or user, see [MOVE](MOVE.HLP).
